Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:43:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] claude: a turn the interactive mode is refused as a
 third-party app's is redone as claude -p (#4503)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Anthropic refuses an interactive Claude Code (the cli entrypoint) a turn
whose prompt is the client agent's own harness prompt — the tools, rules
and skills of Pi, OpenCode and the like, judged as a whole, no phrase of
them alone (#4503's controlled tests). The refusal is a 400 that says
"keep going", and the same request as claude -p is served: its sdk-cli
entrypoint the prompt does not condemn. Until now the 400 reached the
client whole, which is why the bridge looked intermittent.

The bridge holds the reply's start, and on that refusal redoes the turn
once as claude -p: printRetry marks the redo, and a -p run is not redone.
What extra usage the account turns on stays the user's to decide; the
redo runs as claude -p, which the plan counts at about twice the
interactive mode's — spent on a turn that otherwise answered nothing.
Each run's mode is in the log.

